#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347044 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf29db1b-f47b-53de-b31d-e4da1d0a9e5f" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Triple Integral as a Mixed or Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a83c4e86-5ecb-5ab8-ac53-ef7e6fcfb22d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xz" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347046} {:answer/id #uuid "52e2d59b-a700-5f5b-8984-5ce7f5af8b25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347047} {:answer/id #uuid "5eb5f02b-69a0-50cc-a1cd-2961079a75b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347048} {:answer/id #uuid "9473b6c2-2d87-5f21-86fa-1cfa5671c801" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347049} {:answer/id #uuid "3eb74918-959c-5b65-9767-c73a257cca8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9473b6c2-2d87-5f21-86fa-1cfa5671c801" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347049} :answer-field/id #uuid "3082440f-90a7-5f00-948f-05dc52bfa82f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347045}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "02d64a49-09f3-54fa-aded-dbe6a0beb5fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-161712" :question/problem "$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nThe triple integral above is defined over the type III region given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 2x,\\,0\\le y\\le xz}.\n$$\n\nFor a fixed admissible $x$, let $[a(x),b(x)]$ be the full nonempty $z$ fiber of the exactly specified region $S$. What is $a(x)+b(x)$?" :question/worked-solution "The defining set $S$ is retained exactly. The requirement $0\\le z\\le2x$ has no solution for $x<0$, so the actual outer range is $0\\le x\\le2$. For each such $x$, the full $z$ interval is $[0,2x]$, and $xz\\ge0$ makes the $y$ interval $[0,xz]$ nonempty. Hence\n\n$$a(x)+b(x)=0+2x=2x,\\qquad \\iiint_S f\\,dV=\\int_0^2\\int_0^{2x}\\int_0^{xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.$$\n\nFor $f=1$, the true volume is $\\int_0^2 2x^3\\,dx=8$. The source solution retained the nominal outer range $[-1,2]$ and included reversed $z$ bounds on negative $x$, giving the signed value $15/2$. That outer-bound error does not change the requested middle-endpoint sum $2x$."}]}
